[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then we can substitute \(z\) into the expression and simplify.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m First, let's express the given expression in terms of \(\theta\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m = 4((75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m And
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta) + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m = 24(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + 36i(\sin\theta - \cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m = 24\cos\theta + 24i\sin\theta + 36i\sin\theta - 36i\cos\theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m = 24\cos\theta + 60i\sin\theta - 36i\cos\theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m Now we combine these two parts:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m \[
