[36m(TaskRunner pid=1008942)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of finding the amplitude of the expression. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta - b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = 468\), so the maximum value of the real part is:
